{"objects":[{"id":"flow","instance":"instance--b96dad5f-c519-5a1f-a718-912ca4a86c02","objects":["attack-action--1","attack-action--2","attack-action--3","attack-action--4","attack-action--5","attack-action--6","attack-action--7","attack-action--8","attack-action--9","attack-action--10","attack-action--11","attack-condition--1","mutex--1","file--1","file--2","instance--3536a568-610f-5570-bba9-6dfe97bc9c2e","instance--384798bd-a84b-5feb-8d38-7f9d0a087f11","instance--ed6039fe-678b-5ae9-9576-73e6ea35b0c8","instance--7e8c9301-c3f8-55e9-8894-e81f1b6203d9","instance--b6d82c28-0a68-5c6f-b058-c1e072f51852","instance--3622ace1-abf1-5f6e-a5de-a6f584dc1f66","instance--56b40d44-cc57-5e8b-b320-779a685089fd","instance--ede14dbd-ab11-5fb3-876c-d110ff3b2c0b","instance--3bb881aa-a5ab-51ba-b53d-89d26964ce7d","instance--be99ba49-e121-58a8-ba7b-dd3de316cfcf","instance--16ec439e-c0fa-55c2-92d7-f04e66533272","instance--5dd06c90-c780-59da-bdad-de6e85594d0c","instance--3a5ae3c5-7921-5550-aa5d-be3458458401","instance--9ffec466-29ee-5a09-85c7-3fd434d9333f"],"properties":[["name","Embargo ransomware execution flow"],["description","Cyble analyzes the Rust-based Embargo ransomware, investigating its operations and possible variants."],["scope","malware"],["author",[["name","Cyble Research & Intelligence Labs (CRIL)"]]],["external_references",[["item-1",[["source_name","cyble.com"],["url","https://cyble.com/blog/the-rust-revolution-new-embargo-ransomware-steps-in/"]]]]]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--ad592d05-6969-5b51-98a8-1ad9b6aab896","120":"instance--5850a8f4-8241-5e73-9bf0-dcd376cd5025","150":"instance--0da1498f-3beb-5916-a249-e0410a4a81e4","180":"instance--d3632784-7391-5a29-83e2-edab51db56c6","210":"instance--8bc47ca5-ca73-5a04-a9ea-918608f10871","240":"instance--6546eef6-c5ad-516e-a417-89916e651648","270":"instance--244e5a69-f465-564e-9d2c-93d4da44fc57","30":"instance--6a1fca3c-fdb6-536a-bbea-61ac2349a700","300":"instance--043a5b44-2864-5565-abce-1909204e5485","330":"instance--e10eb918-2b0b-56f4-9c82-f345ce21276c","60":"instance--33a99d1b-dad8-51f6-be74-e1614db9151b","90":"instance--380c79e9-b1eb-547c-bf01-a011db1201c1"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--1","properties":[["name","Check command-line arguments"],["description","The behavior of this ransomware can be controlled using command-line arguments. Upon execution, it calls to check for the arguments as shown in the figure below.\n\nIt then checks for the following arguments"],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0002","technique":"T1059"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--4f4d03a8-4502-5010-997b-9943e254395b","120":"instance--cefe62ac-5b6e-5ead-84fc-b4c632913a73","150":"instance--4d07a740-2467-5b95-ac8d-4a2ee8edd11e","180":"instance--1205f03c-a457-5a0b-87ef-3bbb7aac110f","210":"instance--96e7dc6a-9f86-5f69-8d45-a566303cd4c0","240":"instance--66237af6-bb19-5a51-9fa2-cbc4a96186f5","270":"instance--836dfd42-b475-50ca-9acf-4f11bd32b89f","30":"instance--efe92997-cc5c-538a-90bc-c09ffb1379f4","300":"instance--9c4a24ae-1426-5cb5-9d7c-792e6dd325b7","330":"instance--06c6a74a-ca7d-5703-88ea-a06a0933d21a","60":"instance--5e4f84e5-56b7-5b8f-9bc3-b4d59d371123","90":"instance--019deb6a-bab3-57db-9a53-11e3564bf7a4"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--2","properties":[["name","Create mutex"],["description","After getting the command line arguments, the ransomware binary creates a mutex named \u201c \u201d using the function. Unlike other ransomware variants, this one uses a hardcoded mutex name instead of generating a string at runtime. The figure below illustrates the mutex created by the ransomware binary."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0005","technique":"T1622"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--0ce35aea-35a2-52ae-a67b-985306bdefe7","120":"instance--312639d5-e6d9-57b1-850d-28f0a1eac2f6","150":"instance--9551a25e-2558-512e-9894-dd64a8d662bf","180":"instance--403becce-e0ad-5dcd-bc14-7c00453907da","210":"instance--2305f501-2712-5ec6-9d4e-1371b011e937","240":"instance--cf1b8cf6-1cbd-5afb-b653-aa693889dab5","270":"instance--1d3dc59a-40a0-5670-aa3e-1304ff762003","30":"instance--77063d4f-503a-5e9b-b622-15aa2cc6a8e7","300":"instance--beaab67f-8a54-5982-8c5d-9d2ed2d42c9f","330":"instance--4d3274ff-ef14-5a53-99be-01575194a98e","60":"instance--4154a6bf-290b-5fce-a557-5dc0f3e700fb","90":"instance--2992bc0b-df57-54e5-a17b-03a964338c09"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--3","properties":[["name","Clear recycle bin"],["description","Following this, the ransomware proceeds to clear the recycle bin by invoking the function. Typically, this action is taken to hinder the victim\u2019s ability to restore any deleted files after encryption. The figure below shows the ransomware clearing the recycle bin."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0040","technique":"T1490"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--0f6e4da7-a5f4-54d7-866f-3bc6e8bcb019","120":"instance--015254b5-0906-577e-b3e3-3899f837d118","150":"instance--f7af5b8c-330a-58d5-b0da-a3d5f0bc6ad0","180":"instance--9f27ab21-2382-567d-b022-74ad5a29bd08","210":"instance--d799eb0a-7600-5b1a-a298-c47a78ceae4b","240":"instance--911c2c52-5974-5e08-b0b6-a9084d57c6ee","270":"instance--286444b4-97a1-58cd-9ca3-cffa04a15351","30":"instance--92192c38-5143-50e0-8c39-a96ea86e32e2","300":"instance--82bb3de0-bea5-5651-a1de-583283258c6d","330":"instance--4f0945c8-f644-50ce-8796-fea52a29dda1","60":"instance--16c43a2d-7356-521d-a507-5922e2c3337b","90":"instance--abce5c62-339a-5ed5-a0b8-dd66136cfe2f"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--4","properties":[["name","Disable Windows recovery"],["description","Next, it executes the following command to disable the Windows recovery:"],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0040","technique":"T1490"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--a469636c-0cb2-50b9-92f9-644c8aa98197","120":"instance--d57b3a21-e910-5879-8148-40165cea451a","150":"instance--58250ef4-5bb4-5bf3-b33e-89493bbb395d","180":"instance--3e769cf2-c1e5-5d2e-81d4-892f48ce4d86","210":"instance--f6499e41-749c-5d7f-9346-96c08d0d5dfd","240":"instance--d9dcdfc8-5f42-546a-803a-0efcd5d4cf91","270":"instance--c9afd0f6-97ce-57b2-9d60-3557b6214809","30":"instance--75f82155-f5ff-5619-8bf8-aae22937cab0","300":"instance--25e2d26e-1b35-56bd-b9aa-096c2d3b0e3c","330":"instance--e0483688-da10-5376-8cf2-050bcc3b70f0","60":"instance--1293d9cc-16b2-5c67-a453-bd144aab133a","90":"instance--2b43cd52-10db-5b15-8ad5-c4b59496528b"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--5","properties":[["name","Terminate matching processes"],["description","The ransomware then captures a snapshot of active running processes using and iterates over them with and . It checks if any of the processes listed below are running and terminates them if a match is found.\n\nThe figure below illustrates the ransomware iterating through the active processes."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0040","technique":"T1489"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--54fc1f38-f4e3-523e-b07c-73889b0d8df7","120":"instance--9cf45948-7040-5d7a-a1d5-3cb4db0c1af6","150":"instance--13bb13cc-e02b-51d2-8d7d-40e5613b6e5a","180":"instance--e33bc6ee-771e-54fe-a772-74dfdaad420d","210":"instance--286f51a3-8fc6-55ec-978e-8b05ebda3655","240":"instance--14659696-be77-5460-beb1-4b5eac126e43","270":"instance--f48ed1a6-2895-5cd2-9b1c-e30ac2bc8921","30":"instance--7b803e61-16ac-5720-92cd-8f2a456a52b7","300":"instance--76c24361-5143-5c43-8e4d-707c619e6038","330":"instance--f395cfc7-395a-5001-9552-a4fec6dbc53a","60":"instance--760885bb-9294-5a5b-93a2-a410e1ea4112","90":"instance--8e0d1a12-8611-598d-9a7d-40f2525e4781"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--6","properties":[["name","Stop matching services"],["description","After this, the ransomware retrieves the active services running on the victim\u2019s system. It first calls the function to obtain a handle to the service control manager database. Then, it calls to enumerate the services in the service control manager database. This call retrieves the status of services, including their names and current states. The ransomware then checks if any of the running services match the following services:\n\nIf a match is found, it closes the service by calling the function. The figure below illustrates the ransomware iterating through services."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0040","technique":"T1489"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--7cccbcd0-a724-54fb-be4f-ac523d26f7d0","120":"instance--738e44b2-1357-5eb3-82bd-8a0ce8942b72","150":"instance--d31f4735-6339-5929-8d7c-d30863cf166f","180":"instance--2252393d-d801-5931-ad38-4b53374a9880","210":"instance--065b5ad5-023a-5336-b458-e9c9dcda2976","240":"instance--5ea0dd2b-5eac-51f8-855a-4cbcb801bc2d","270":"instance--bba66874-a069-56c6-bb95-967cb3cefc9e","30":"instance--6377c09d-ecb4-5567-a2f4-4dde56ff4f98","300":"instance--ede3430f-b16b-58ae-be71-1d1f1a194336","330":"instance--7772f482-8ee2-569a-b600-7528c065d4e0","60":"instance--98139a98-16b0-54fe-8c77-3473c1b520cd","90":"instance--5cb9cc95-e190-5a68-985d-0a94d39299e6"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--7","properties":[["name","Enumerate device volumes"],["description","The ransomware now starts iterating through device volumes using the and functions. It then calls the function to retrieve a list of drive letters and mounted folder paths for each specified volume.\n\nFigure 12 \u2013 Fetching Drives"],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0007","technique":"T1120"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--5150f7cc-6f25-5eb3-a6fc-5099ced4caf4","120":"instance--64a408ce-c543-55d6-a9dd-206ce7cadbb2","150":"instance--1b71e413-cfd2-528c-8792-dc7dd1bb9938","180":"instance--aa12ce11-0165-52b6-b72d-e4d9070e9fbb","210":"instance--5d8b0f08-14bc-58f4-9316-b25a92dd09a6","240":"instance--34f96b84-9453-53f2-ae07-d28c04665e6c","270":"instance--415f1d54-1cd4-5ba7-8071-4aa99bc946ac","30":"instance--18834cac-b4c4-57b0-88ea-5a62fdb27cf9","300":"instance--de4f9957-1ac6-5782-86ea-f1a3b6a9ad13","330":"instance--8eff940b-86bb-556f-8c85-c7c47577b3ed","60":"instance--14a123fd-5626-5e69-8257-6dcd64c28ec0","90":"instance--02294ff1-7261-5db8-8e0d-b9e818922053"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--8","properties":[["name","Enumerate network resources and files"],["description","After this, it uses the function to enumerate the network resources. It then starts enumerating the files in the drives for encryption using and, and functions, as shown in the figure below."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0007","technique":"T1135"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--180f2983-9c1a-56f4-99d6-c990125f7baa","120":"instance--c7f65318-7600-57f4-a8ac-992357e695ff","150":"instance--95523e1a-0a1d-52ef-944c-23f9cbc50233","180":"instance--bc8eb48d-411d-5877-aa9b-966476b71207","210":"instance--4cc5026e-07f9-5327-9912-5d278a0a3321","240":"instance--d6a7d51d-39a4-5eb3-8831-f23437781b95","270":"instance--cac30e05-5f01-5b4f-b5c0-6b975297df2d","30":"instance--cb0751b0-c027-5895-a460-a72e48920c71","300":"instance--f41cdc1f-abb7-5ff7-81c2-bf2235a7faab","330":"instance--b114cbda-9ec8-5612-b2f8-93c36811cafb","60":"instance--f28e5296-2041-5fe9-992d-4c70d549191e","90":"instance--3ea39244-da0f-5435-8745-f2afa8b13872"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--9","properties":[["name","Encrypt files with ChaCha20 and Curve25519"],["description","This ransomware uses ChaCha20 and Curve25519 to encrypt files, as shown in the figure below. ChaCha20 and Curve25519 are often used together in file encryption to provide secure key exchange and encryption. Curve25519 establishes a shared secret key, which is then used by ChaCha20 to encrypt and decrypt the file contents."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0040","technique":"T1486"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--db5fab04-54d4-5eec-a429-185861eb2719","120":"instance--985391bd-d017-5935-ab31-3b4b56331b02","150":"instance--092bb98d-fc30-5f69-b6b7-e3024f3ec65a","180":"instance--755129e6-612e-5b63-a780-1c886d98909b","210":"instance--431723d9-dd8c-5190-9dab-6f346173c044","240":"instance--5b9fb821-54fe-5f22-bba3-038263245910","270":"instance--3c6777cb-6430-544b-b31a-01b198524553","30":"instance--c070071b-a9a3-52fe-8956-a51744db200b","300":"instance--a9a4289c-d995-5783-9544-a8b45052eb56","330":"instance--344009cc-e024-5c68-9246-51e85e00d45c","60":"instance--86c77621-2c1d-59c3-b398-e62f4b48a3dd","90":"instance--67627b08-1913-5f3d-8318-52d3bda9c1c3"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--10","properties":[["name","Drop ransom note"],["description","Next, the ransomware drops a ransom note named \u201cHOW_TO_RECOVER_FILES.txt\u201d in every directory it iterates through. This note appears to be created specific to a victim, as date and time values are hardcoded rather than dynamically loading the current date and time."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0040","technique":"T1486"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--6b7baffd-afaf-5472-9af2-a263119a77ef","120":"instance--83f38e63-e29a-53f4-99d9-927a195c453f","150":"instance--3e720145-b7a1-5bd6-8a7d-bb13519675d1","180":"instance--bdce060f-d96c-5b06-b8f4-1ab1527fd01d","210":"instance--a4feb251-e6e3-5680-a712-d59c92f73ccf","240":"instance--9a564ca6-b753-5b06-880c-b3aac25c1e73","270":"instance--76861a89-f006-5e0d-8c5b-ebdcb5e926dc","30":"instance--cf41e64d-4a4b-58d9-9962-72d278b2c489","300":"instance--ac1d6edd-482f-5f13-9348-b605afcc260c","330":"instance--ed78dfa1-f300-564f-b2cd-6c99552b9a68","60":"instance--979accb3-1b3e-5af4-9182-78392cbaf904","90":"instance--ae721c42-320e-5ea4-9c77-339a05b6e12f"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--11","properties":[["name","Append encrypted file extension"],["description","All the encrypted files consist of \u201c.564ba1\u201d as a file extension, as shown in the figure below."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0040","technique":"T1486"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--35652c79-2c41-5d60-81ba-b5e47aa554bf","120":"instance--53906203-fffb-5af3-b112-44a9b4b49b8f","150":"instance--465fbc8a-7b4c-569f-be00-c0fbc137fcfc","180":"instance--a653c96b-3673-5dfa-968e-188fffe4cc04","210":"instance--6a344cf5-bd5c-52db-84f5-23c7701c7a5e","30":"instance--913561d1-b5f3-54d2-8272-159233dfde54","330":"instance--d59fe52d-c897-5f3a-919a-c2273cb8a8b3","60":"instance--f1fd6a3d-bb83-543d-a379-39d4632978f7","90":"instance--4cd6fce2-0d24-57f0-b161-12a867cd1100","branch:False":"instance--f7e897b3-3607-5ea5-8d15-5f83ba8a60da","branch:True":"instance--39b5ac19-b0dd-5674-a7d9-d75e659fe9ea"},"id":"condition","instance":"attack-condition--1","properties":[["description","The ransomware does not encrypt files present in the following directories on an infected system. The ransomware binary contains regular expressions for these directory names.\n\nAlso, this ransomware does not encrypt files with the following extensions. The list includes the \u201c.564ba1\u201d extension, which is appended to files after encryption. This ensures that the ransomware will not encrypt the same file twice."]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--3efdb833-7f3d-5300-805b-987582ae48cf","120":"instance--42a0b9c8-cbda-5096-ade5-6e023140ed17","150":"instance--006329ef-f22d-5b67-b636-f5b570a8a96e","180":"instance--4611f129-5963-58a8-be89-b11ed3b7b8c6","210":"instance--4a8f47bb-d938-56ae-8cbd-48845700bd26","240":"instance--4bda4043-889f-50a8-ad67-b32a1143ed12","270":"instance--c46f3601-8189-5732-b6f1-aa347a3e49d0","30":"instance--27a629d4-b66b-51a1-8bcc-c21dc5e39af5","300":"instance--5a144b8e-4d9b-5613-b971-e9116065b713","330":"instance--b3f8afa8-0530-5bcf-af61-92b907a4c3a6","60":"instance--5b2ec8aa-5a01-592e-89b2-dd5be70ce8a6","90":"instance--61e0f1d9-5421-531d-a664-5162b4bbf912"},"id":"mutex","instance":"mutex--1","properties":[["value"," "],["evidence",[["item-1",{"excerpt":"After getting the command line arguments, the ransomware binary creates a mutex named \u201c \u201d using the function.","source":"https://cyble.com/blog/the-rust-revolution-new-embargo-ransomware-steps-in/","source_field":"normalized_text"}]]],["display_name","hardcoded mutex name"],["name","hardcoded mutex name"]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--8cf549a5-7e7d-51cf-9368-9b5e0744592a","120":"instance--06d4fda8-e0bf-574e-b3d8-a62c44712794","150":"instance--bb5815b3-6a43-5e3f-b9bc-9862b25fcfbb","180":"instance--f044d6bc-5582-5c4b-8062-d78469e24a48","210":"instance--e728313e-5605-515c-b37b-9ffb6e4816de","240":"instance--2e67ae43-8ff1-546b-b53a-2147995d4ec2","270":"instance--9f6cbb4c-d86c-53ed-890d-a560dca0b584","30":"instance--3bed1646-ea3a-5567-b439-b19993f3bb89","300":"instance--eaaf034a-e88c-5110-84f3-b644fd9af752","330":"instance--1f54afc1-8d53-569a-9f5a-625de523f9b0","60":"instance--e5c6eb85-2474-59e2-b136-a99f7e8c85a3","90":"instance--f4164786-5d40-5ba5-9ff1-764895cce7f5"},"id":"file","instance":"file--1","properties":[["value","HOW_TO_RECOVER_FILES.txt"],["evidence",[["item-1",{"excerpt":"Next, the ransomware drops a ransom note named \u201cHOW_TO_RECOVER_FILES.txt\u201d in every directory it iterates through.","source":"https://cyble.com/blog/the-rust-revolution-new-embargo-ransomware-steps-in/","source_field":"normalized_text"}]]],["display_name","HOW_TO_RECOVER_FILES.txt"],["name","HOW_TO_RECOVER_FILES.txt"]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--3e66a567-5f6a-55f7-bf7d-c2b321c465a9","120":"instance--723c477a-612e-5e7e-abf6-92e3f839a0e4","150":"instance--d5db6df5-d592-52e6-bbe2-c2b204fd3f2e","180":"instance--d7d9e810-de60-5c28-9cdd-f46fa6fac092","210":"instance--78b33a09-4062-5f1b-8e0a-938bf8e943c4","240":"instance--5fc7788c-2e04-580d-81de-5c2b7dacc94f","270":"instance--c62d1543-dc41-5f2f-9d36-5ead3de62016","30":"instance--7b4f278c-c194-50e8-9a85-7e914f1d454f","300":"instance--bf78f6c5-df99-56cb-aecb-17157d5d408a","330":"instance--b993e222-e5fb-52f0-8beb-035a5c5a81a3","60":"instance--5bc53f6b-461d-53a7-8d43-45ba723876f3","90":"instance--c94e773c-3b0c-5d29-9aa2-f48fef02b68d"},"id":"file","instance":"file--2","properties":[["extensions",[["item-1",".564ba1"]]],["evidence",[["item-1",{"excerpt":"All the encrypted files consist of \u201c.564ba1\u201d as a file extension, as shown in the figure below.","source":"https://cyble.com/blog/the-rust-revolution-new-embargo-ransomwar